     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nAcetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg a day. That is more than twice the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg a day (many services use 3,000 mg a day). A single 3,000 mg dose is also three times the usual 1,000 mg maximum. A dose this high risks serious hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily**, which is 3,000 mg a day.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, which is 2,600 mg a day.\n- **1,000 mg PO every 6 hours**, which is 4,000 mg a day. This is the ceiling, so use it only if the team wants it.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. Please also check the intended order with your resident or attending or with pharmacy."
      }
     ],
