      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily delivers 9,000 mg a day. That is a potentially lethal dose and carries a real risk of acute liver failure. Normal liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't make it safe.\n\nIt's possible something got garbled, such as a units mix-up or a different intended dose. Here's what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a safe dose right away.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg a day), or 1,000 mg PO every 6 hours (4,000 mg a day, the maximum).\n- **Add a note to the order** if you want one, such as \"max 3 g/24 h from all sources.\"\n- **Help you check with your resident, attending, or pharmacy.** If someone with prescribing authority really intends this dose, they should confirm it directly. I'd still expect pharmacy to stop it.\n\nWhich dose and frequency should I enter?"
      }
     ],
